## 2026-11-09: Native scripted evidence is separate from submission model evidence

- Scope: publication of the native dual-Panda candidate tasks. Preserve native
  development evidence; do not infer a model-route exception from non-YAM status.
- Current upstream AGENTS requires Dream-1 video for two parallel-gripper arms,
  with an Inspect LLM alternative stated for other robots. Dual Panda fits the
  former morphology. A native Inspect script or ordinary LLM run alone does not
  establish compliance with that requirement.
- Dream's public adapter binds to YAM `joint_pos`, six joints plus gripper per
  arm, YAM labels and station cameras. Native Panda's fourteen EEF pose/jaw
  coordinates have different semantics. Renaming fields is not a valid bridge.
- Publication is authorized by the latest user request, but the three selected
  native candidates currently lack actual compliant model evidence and retain
  scorer/construct/novelty gaps. No incomplete placeholder or mislabeled video
  was published. Once eligible, no redundant publication permission is needed.
- Evidence: upstream AGENTS fetched2026-11-09, kairosiann/inspect-robots-dream
  policy.py and _station.py; artifacts/submission-prep/round1/publication-preflight.json;
  docs/porting/BREV_VALIDATION.md and docs/porting/INSPECT.md.

